 rebuilt as native Elementor modules.</p>", "text_color": "#a6a49d", "typography_typography": "custom", "typography_font_family": "Inter", "_title": "Article deck"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "883d2b1", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "image", "settings": {"image": {"url": "https://www.lovart.ai/assets/use-cases/social-media/how-to.png", "id": "", "alt": "Thumbnail design science"}, "image_size": "full", "caption_source": "none", "_title": "Article hero image"}, "elements": []}], "isInner": true}], "isInner": false}, {"id": "29d1fc0", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 28, "sizes": []}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "80", "right": "40", "bottom": "80", "left": "40", "isLinked": false}, "margin": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "0", "isLinked": true}, "background_background": "classic", "background_color": "#100f09", "css_classes": "lr dark lr-native lr-native-article-body", "_title": "LR Native — Blog Body"}, "elements": [{"id": "84a406d", "elType": "container", "settings": {"content_width": "full", "flex_direction": "column", "gap": {"unit": "px", "size": 20, "sizes": []}, "padding": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "0", "isLinked": true}, "margin": {"unit": "px", "top": "0", "right": "0", "bottom": "0", "left": "0", "isLinked": true}, "css_classes": "lr-native-article-flow"}, "elements": [{"id": "45f39f6", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Start with contrast, not decoration", "header_size": "h2", "title_color": "#f7f6f2", "typography_typography": "custom", "typography_font_family": "Inter", "_title": "Section heading"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "4b1334b", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Thumbnails are judged at 120 pixels wide. At that size only two things survive: a strong value contrast between subject and background, and at most three words of text. Everything else is noise the feed will swallow.</p>", "text_color": "#a6a49d", "typography_typography": "custom", "typography_font_family": "Inter", "_title": "Paragraph"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "e35a965", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "Faces beat objects — most of the time", "header_size": "h2", "title_color": "#f7f6f2", "typography_typography": "custom", "typography_font_family": "Inter", "_title": "Section heading"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "f310c8e", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>A cropped, expressive face consistently outperforms static product shots on CTR. But the face must earn its place: one emotion, exaggerated, lit against a background it contrasts with. Two competing faces halve the signal.</p>", "text_color": "#a6a49d", "typography_typography": "custom", "typography_font_family": "Inter", "_title": "Paragraph"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "882558d", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>Test the silhouette: blur the design until only shapes remain. If the composition still reads — one subject, one focal accent — it will survive the feed. If it turns to mush, no amount of detail will save it.</p>", "text_color": "#a6a49d", "typography_typography": "custom", "typography_font_family": "Inter", "_title": "Paragraph"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "7a55402", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "heading", "settings": {"title": "The three-word rule", "header_size": "h2", "title_color": "#f7f6f2", "typography_typography": "custom", "typography_font_family": "Inter", "_title": "Section heading"}, "elements": []}, {"id": "baf5aef", "elType": "widget", "widgetType": "text-editor", "settings": {"editor": "<p>On-thumbnail text is a hook, not a headline. Pick the three words that create the open loop, set them in one weight, and let the title in the feed do the explaining.</p>", "text_color": "#a6a49d", "typography_typography": "custom", "typo